35,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,The transport receipts show a 38% cost spike for distant trips. I need to know exactly where that money went before we commit to anything.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Toshio,,The hall is booked by three other clubs. Splitting training into early mornings and late evenings is unacceptable. We need a continuous block.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The seniors confirm mixing only happens when we share a building. Also, a third of us need a bed to make the nine o'clock start.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"The attendance sheets show a fifth never came, mostly gone by winter. The rate sheet lists 1,100 yen per night, including equipment.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The rate sheet confirms 1,100 yen per night, all-inclusive. However, the inland accounts show eight-to-a-room sleeping. That density makes cost-sharing impossible to verify fairly.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Asuka, eight-to-a-room explains the cost gap. I need to see if the transport receipts match the actual distance we traveled.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Ryuji, the transport spike is irrelevant if we stay local. The canteen closure means self-cooking costs two hours daily. We need staffed kitchens to protect training time.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Toshio, self-cooking eats the very evenings we need for mixing. We need a location that solves both the schedule and the social isolation.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Toshio, I agree. The 1,100 yen rate includes equipment, so we avoid self-cooking. This protects our sleep and training time.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Toshio, self-cooking creates untrackable side expenses. I need a flat, verifiable fee structure to ensure the total cost is distributed fairly among all members.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Toshio, I agree. The 1,100 yen rate is verifiable. I will not accept untrackable side expenses. We need a flat, auditable fee structure to close the account gap.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
